Summary: Keep a click in a fullscreen Space from reaching the window's frame view
Category: input
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: after Second Chance's workaround (it swizzles the same method)
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/)
Why: Wine takes a click in -[WineApplicationController handleEvent:], before
 AppKit dispatches it, and then lets NSApplication deliver it as well. It
 goes to the window's WineContentView, which had no mouseDown:, so it went
 on up the responder chain to the window's frame view (NSThemeFrame). In a
 fullscreen Space the frame view starts dragging the fullscreen window from
 wherever the click is, and that drag sets the arrow cursor in place of the
 program's own. WineContentView now takes mouseDown: and, while the window
 is in a fullscreen Space, drops it; otherwise it passes it on as before.
 mouseDownCanMoveWindow (already NO for every Wine view) doesn't help: the
 frame view only asks it for drags from the title bar or a textured
 background.
 A debug build showed the click reaching -[WineContentView mouseDown:] in a
 fullscreen Space, with the window's NSThemeFrame as its next responder;
 with this change the program still gets the press, moves and release of
 a drag.
Programs: Webmaster (Tivola; cnc-ddraw, its own glove cursor), plain Wine
 with EmulateModeset in a fullscreen Space: a click anywhere in the picture
 turned the glove into the Mac's arrow until the game next set its cursor
 (Second Chance, 2026-11-12)
Uncertain: The arrow without the patch was seen by Second Chance, not here.
 Other buttons (rightMouseDown:, otherMouseDown:) still go up the chain.
No test: needs a fullscreen Space and a live cursor to look at (a
 background login has none)
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-22: confirmed on a console with host14 (watched by
 the user): Webmaster in a fullscreen Space, plain driver, Second Chance's
 workaround off: the glove cursor stayed through clicks (1 session).

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -354,6 +354,16 @@
 @implementation WineContentView
 
 @synthesize everHadGLContext = _everHadGLContext;
+
+    - (void) mouseDown:(NSEvent*)theEvent
+    {
+        /* Wine has already taken the click, in -[WineApplicationController
+         * handleEvent:]. Passed on up the responder chain, in a fullscreen Space
+         * it reaches the window's frame view, which starts dragging the window
+         * from wherever the click was and sets the arrow cursor. */
+        if (!([[self window] styleMask] & NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen))
+            [super mouseDown:theEvent];
+    }
 
     - (instancetype) initWithFrame:(NSRect)frame
     {
